																		Author Overview
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/weizhong" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1777811); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1777811&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606834480" alt="weizhong" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1777811)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/weizhong" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1777811); return false;" >weizhong</a></span> <span class="odate time_1533097112 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">01 Aug 2018 04:18</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3893411">
									

<hr />
<div style="text-align: center;">
<p><em>I fear all we have done is to awaken a sleeping giant and fill him with a terrible resolve.</em><br /></p>
<div style="text-align: right;">
<p>- Isoroku Yamamoto, <em>Tora! Tora! Tora!</em> (1980)</p>
</div>
</div>
<hr />
<p>It's good to be back.</p>
<p>This is the longest work that I've ever published for this site, and definitely the most ambitious. I hope you enjoy reading it as much as I did writing it.</p>
<p>I must thank a phenomenal cast of reviewers who greatly assisted me in this process, whether it was providing detailed advice, or simply reading it when I asked.</p>
<ul>
<li>Many thanks to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/riemann" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1787775); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1787775&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1533099178" alt="Riemann" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1787775)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/riemann" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1787775); return false;">Riemann</a></span> for his initial reviewing of the earliest stages of my draft, and for providing a wonderful voice into writing style.</li>
<li><span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/a-random-day" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1841781); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1841781&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1533099178" alt="A Random Day" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1841781)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/a-random-day" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1841781); return false;">A Random Day</a></span> was critical for refining this into the version that you see now, as well as giving me the inspiration for the title.</li>
<li><span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/modern-erasmus" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3129691); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3129691&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1533099178" alt="Modern_Erasmus" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3129691)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/modern-erasmus" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3129691); return false;">Modern_Erasmus</a></span> was very helpful for his insight into the subtler points of the draft, which helped me guide my overall vision.</li>
<li>Additionally, the lovely reviewers of the SCPD Discord were great readers whenever I bugged them.</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Stray&nbsp;Observations</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Stray&nbsp;Observations</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<ul>
<li><strong><em>Kagemusha</em></strong> - Literally translated, this is &quot;Shadow Warrior,&quot; but in Japanese, it's used as the term for a political decoy. More abstractly, it refers to a 1980 film by Akira Kurosawa that centered around the concept.</li>
<li>Unit 731 was, in fact, a terrifyingly <strong>real</strong> institution that did in fact commit all of the war crimes that I used as a background for the Pingfang 5. <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unit_731">Learn more here!</a></li>
<li>A strong basis for this skip was my interest in WW2 Japanese holdouts, who were a very real phenomenon whereby numerous Japanese soldiers refused to stand down following the war. <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese_holdout">Learn more here!</a></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<hr />
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Image&nbsp;Attributions</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Image&nbsp;Attributions</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Image 1, the Pingfang 5 itself, is from <a href="http://www.flickriver.com/photos/14684508@N02/sets/72157624302723961/">this Flickr collection, which is CC compliant.</a></p>
<p>Image 2, the IJAMEA ensign, is from the <a href="/ijamea-hub">IJAMEA Hub</a>, on the site itself.</p>
<p>Image 3, of Director Shiro Ishii, is from <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shir%C5%8D_Ishii">Wikimedia Commons, and is public domain.</a></p>
<p>Image 4, SCP-4000-1, is from <a href="http://histomil.com/viewtopic.php?t=3918&amp;start=5140">This history website, and was labeled for reuse.</a></p>
<p>Image 5, SCP-4000-2, is from <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shoichi_Yokoi">Wikimedia Commons, and is public domain.</a> Fun fact: the image is Shoichi Yokoi, a real life Japanese holdout!</p>
<p>Image 6, SCP-4000-3, is from <a href="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/81/NRA_soldiers_and_shoes_made_of_straw.jpg">Wikimedia Commons as well.</a></p>
<p>Image 7, SCP-4000-4, is from <a href="http://www.ww2incolor.com/japan/C__pia+de+C+paratroopers+_25_.html">this WW2 photo website, and was labeled for reuse.</a></p>
<p>Image 8, the map of the Southeast Asian Ocean, is <a href="http://www.geographicguide.net/asia/southeast-political.htm">public domain as well</a>, and then modified by myself.</p>
<p>Image 9, the divers, is a photo from <a href="https://www.nps.gov/bisc/learn/historyculture/maritime-heritage-trail.htm">the US National Park Service website</a>, and is public domain.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

